wayland95 (0.5.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New: Wayland Studio (Start > Programs > Programming), for making your own Wayland 95 programs: tables with their rules in SQLite, MySQL or PostgreSQL, forms drawn on a grid, code for their events, graphs (stock graphs too), sound and video, web APIs as tables, an AI chat, and a program of its own at the end. Its manual (F1) opens in the new Markdown Reader. Fixes: a screen capture could come back empty on Intel graphics; a drop-down list opened inside a dialog was drawn under it.

 -- Wayland 95 <wayland95@localhost>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:35:43 -0800

wayland95 (0.4.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New: a Web Browser (the Chromium engine) with tabs, favorites, history, downloads, saved passwords in your keyring and private windows; Email (IMAP and SMTP); a Calculator (Standard and Scientific); a Markdown Editor; Backup to a USB drive on a schedule (Control Panel > Backup); Start Up (login programs, systemd services, boot); USB drives in My Computer and the tray, with Open and Eject; and in Control Panel > Services: MySQL (MariaDB), SQLite and the nginx Web Server.

 -- Wayland 95 <wayland95@localhost>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:02:00 -0800

wayland95 (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New: Solitaire and Mines (Start > Programs > Games), Find: All Files (Start > Find), a Matrix screen saver, a bigger Start menu (Control Panel > Taskbar: Start menu size), WireGuard in Control Panel > Services, IP details and a VPN padlock in the network icon, program icons on taskbar buttons, time zones in Date/Time, and right-click menus on My Computer and the Recycle Bin. Fixes: X11 programs such as LibreOffice could end the desktop; dialogs now stay in front of their window.

 -- Wayland 95 <wayland95@localhost>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:50:03 -0800

wayland95 (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The desktop is now wayland95-compositor (wlroots) with win95shell, replacing the Qt compositor: GPU buffer sharing, popups and input as other desktops do them, a real lock screen, two or more displays, and display settings (resolution, refresh rate, scale, orientation, arrangement) in Control Panel > Display. Faster window frames and resizing.

 -- Wayland 95 <wayland95@localhost>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:02:56 -0500

